1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,056
Forty-nine bank statement lines.

2
00:00:02,056 --> 00:00:06,683
Claude built my budget in thirty-four seconds, in its head, to the cent.

3
00:00:06,683 --> 00:00:09,960
But the real spreadsheet it made for me had a trap.

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:10,932
The test:

5
00:00:10,932 --> 00:00:14,368
my October statement, forty-nine transactions.

6
00:00:14,368 --> 00:00:17,206
Salary, rent, groceries, fuel, coffee.

7
00:00:17,206 --> 00:00:18,103
One request:

8
00:00:18,103 --> 00:00:22,360
totals by category, money in, money out, and the balance.

9
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:27,535
By hand, you have to sort all forty-nine lines, then write one formula per category.

10
00:00:27,535 --> 00:00:30,910
I checked every total with code, so I had the right answer.

11
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:31,828
First try:

12
00:00:31,828 --> 00:00:34,364
Claude, no spreadsheet, just in the chat.

13
00:00:34,364 --> 00:00:35,601
Thirty-four seconds.

14
00:00:35,601 --> 00:00:36,158
Money in:

15
00:00:36,158 --> 00:00:39,250
two thousand four hundred ninety-two euros thirty.

16
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:39,868
Money out:

17
00:00:39,868 --> 00:00:42,280
two thousand seventy-eight twenty-nine.

18
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:42,775
Balance:

19
00:00:42,775 --> 00:00:45,620
plus four hundred fourteen euros and one cent.

20
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,754
I compare it with my check:

21
00:00:47,754 --> 00:00:48,569
all correct.

22
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:49,385
To the cent.

23
00:00:49,385 --> 00:00:52,442
I ran it twice more, once with a small model:

24
00:00:52,442 --> 00:00:54,140
three times, zero errors.

25
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,071
Second try:

26
00:00:56,071 --> 00:00:57,829
I ask for a real Excel file.

27
00:00:57,829 --> 00:00:58,959
Fifty-one seconds.

28
00:00:58,959 --> 00:01:04,170
A Statement sheet with categories, a Budget sheet with SUMIF formulas, and a chart.

29
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:08,006
I open it in a spreadsheet app:

30
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:11,655
same totals, plus a check row that adds everything up again.

31
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:12,020
Clean.

32
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,864
Then I add a November expense at the bottom of the statement.

33
00:01:15,864 --> 00:01:17,316
Fifty euros of groceries.

34
00:01:17,316 --> 00:01:18,710
The budget doesn't move.

35
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:19,688
The reason:

36
00:01:19,688 --> 00:01:21,721
every formula stops at row fifty.

37
00:01:21,721 --> 00:01:25,540
Anything added below is ignored, with no error message at all.

38
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,604
The fix is one sentence added to the request:

39
00:01:28,604 --> 00:01:32,350
use whole columns or an Excel table, so new rows get counted.

40
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:34,142
Verdict:

41
00:01:34,142 --> 00:01:36,187
on the math, Claude made no mistakes.

42
00:01:36,187 --> 00:01:40,000
On the file, check the formula ranges before you reuse it next month.
